# L2 technical vocabulary: what was observed, from which source, and when it stops
# being worth believing.
#
# L2 is not a second business layer. Every term below exists because a technical fact
# is only true as of the last time somebody looked, so an L2 statement that cannot say
# who looked and when is not a weaker fact - it is not a fact at all. That is the whole
# difference from ontology/biz.ttl, where a statement is true because the organization
# declared it and stays true until the organization declares otherwise.
#
# Exactly one term crosses between the layers, and it points upward: tech:realizes
# says a technical artifact delivers a business capability. There is no downward term
# and there will not be one, because a capability has to survive the deletion of every
# system that ever delivered it (docs/l1-business-layer.md).
#
# Freshness is materialized, never computed at read time. tech:freshUntil is an
# instant the reconciler wrote down, so a consumer asks "is my instant before it?" and
# compares two timestamps. Nothing here invites duration arithmetic, which SPARQL
# engines disagree about and which fails open (docs/evolution.md).
#
# Enforcement is SHACL, not a reasoner. rdfs:domain and rdfs:range below are
# documentation for external consumers; no inference is ever run over this vocabulary.

@prefix biz:  <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/biz#> .
@prefix tech: <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Semantic layer technical vocabulary (L2)" ;
    rdfs:comment "Observed technical truth: sources, observations, and the artifacts one observation attributes." ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" ;
    owl:imports <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/core> .

## Provenance: the three things every observed fact hangs off.

tech:Source
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "Source" ;
    rdfs:comment """A system observations are read from, at one installation of it. The source is the
scope every identifier it contributes is minted under, so github.com and a GitHub Enterprise host are
two sources and their identical numeric ids never collide. See docs/identifiers.md.""" .

tech:Observation
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "Observation" ;
    rdfs:comment """One act of reading one source at one instant. Every imported entity points at
exactly one of these, which is what makes an L2 fact answerable for: without it a reader has a claim
about a system and no way to ask when it was last true.""" .

tech:Artifact
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "Artifact" ;
    rdfs:comment "Anything imported from a source. The superclass exists so provenance and the layer boundary are stated once, for every kind of thing a source can name." .

tech:Account
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:label "Account" ;
    rdfs:comment """An account at the source: on GitHub, a user or an organization. It is not an
Actor. An account is who the source says pushed something; who the organization holds accountable is
an L1 decision nothing here is allowed to make.""" .

tech:Repository
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:label "Repository" ;
    rdfs:comment "A source-controlled repository at the source, identified by the immutable id the source issued it rather than by the path it is reachable at today." .

tech:Branch
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:subClassOf tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:label "Branch" ;
    rdfs:comment """A named line of development in one repository. GitHub issues a branch no
immutable id, and git has none to issue: a branch is its name within its repository, and renaming
one is a delete and a create. So a branch identifier carries both, and a rename is a different
branch rather than the same one under a new name.""" .

## Source attributes.

tech:provider
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "provider" ;
    rdfs:comment "Which kind of system this source is, as a slug: 'github'. Half of the scope every identifier from this source is minted under." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Source ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:apiRoot
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "API root" ;
    rdfs:comment "The endpoint this source was read from. Which installation of the provider was observed is not a detail: two of them issue the same ids for different things." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Source ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI .

tech:trustBasis
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "trust basis" ;
    rdfs:comment """Why a consumer should believe what this source said, in one sentence: what was
read, with whose authority, and what that authority does not cover. A pack carries this so trust is
a stated claim a reader can weigh rather than an assumption they inherit.""" ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Source ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

## Observation attributes.

tech:observedFrom
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "observed from" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this observation was made by reading that source. Exactly one, because an observation spanning two sources cannot be reproduced from either." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Observation ;
    rdfs:range tech:Source .

tech:observedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "observed at" ;
    rdfs:comment "The instant the source was read. Not the instant the result was committed; git records that." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Observation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

tech:freshUntil
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "fresh until" ;
    rdfs:comment """The instant after which this observation is stale. Materialized when the
observation is reconciled, so asking whether a fact is fresh is a comparison of two timestamps and
never duration arithmetic - which SPARQL engines disagree about and which fails open.""" ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Observation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

tech:snapshotDigest
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "snapshot digest" ;
    rdfs:comment "The SHA-256 of the captured response this observation was reconciled from, as 'sha256:<hex>'. It is what makes the graph checkable against the bytes it came from." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Observation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:observationTarget
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "observation target" ;
    rdfs:comment "What was asked for, in the source's own terms: 'vvonkledge/siana'. A consumer expecting one target and handed another can tell." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Observation ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

## Artifact attributes.

tech:observedIn
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "observed in" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this artifact is what that observation saw. Exactly one, because an artifact attributed to two observations has two answers to 'when was this last true'." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:range tech:Observation .

tech:sourceLocalId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "source local id" ;
    rdfs:comment """The name this artifact has inside its source, kept verbatim so an identifier
minted here can be traced back to the thing it was minted from. It is meaningless without the source,
which is why it is never an identifier on its own.""" ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:webUrl
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "web URL" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where a person can go and look at this artifact. Reported by the source, so it is constrained to https rather than believed." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:range xsd:anyURI .

tech:realizes
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "realizes" ;
    rdfs:comment """Read: this technical artifact delivers that business capability. The only edge
that crosses between the layers, and it points upward, from the thing that decays to the thing that
does not. It is authored by a human under review and never imported: a source knows what it contains,
not what the organization is accountable for. There is no downward term, because a capability outlives
every system that ever delivered it.""" ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Artifact ;
    rdfs:range biz:Capability .

## Account attributes.

tech:accountLogin
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "account login" ;
    rdfs:comment "The account's handle at the source. Renameable, which is exactly why it is an attribute and not the identifier." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Account ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

## Repository attributes.

tech:ownedByAccount
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "owned by account" ;
    rdfs:comment """Read: the source says this repository sits under that account. This is the
source's own containment and nothing more. It is not biz:ownedBy, it names no Actor, and no
accountability follows from it.""" ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range tech:Account .

tech:defaultBranch
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "default branch" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this branch is where the repository sends a reader who names none. It has to be a branch the same observation saw, or the observation is incomplete." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range tech:Branch .

tech:repositoryPath
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "repository path" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where the repository is reachable today, as 'owner/name'. Renameable in one click, which is why it is an attribute: a rename rewrites this and leaves the identifier alone." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:visibility
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "visibility" ;
    rdfs:comment "What the source says about who may read this repository: 'public', 'private', 'internal'." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:primaryLanguage
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "primary language" ;
    rdfs:comment "The language the source reports most of the repository is written in. Absent where the source reports none, rather than guessed." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:archived
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "archived" ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the source has marked the repository read-only." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .

tech:pushedAt
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "pushed at" ;
    rdfs:comment "When the source last saw a push. A fact about the repository, not about the observation: it is why an old observation of a quiet repository can still be worth reading." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Repository ;
    rdfs:range xsd:dateTime .

## Branch attributes.

tech:branchOf
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "branch of" ;
    rdfs:comment "Read: this branch belongs to that repository. Exactly one, because a branch name only identifies anything within one repository." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Branch ;
    rdfs:range tech:Repository .

tech:branchName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "branch name" ;
    rdfs:comment "The branch's name, verbatim. It is half of the branch's identity rather than a display label, and it is carried as an attribute too so a reader never has to decode an identifier to get it back." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Branch ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:headCommit
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "head commit" ;
    rdfs:comment "The commit the branch pointed at when it was observed, as a 40-character SHA-1. The one field here that says what the observation actually saw rather than how it was arranged." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Branch ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string .

tech:protected
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://semantic-layer.19h09.co/vocab/tech> ;
    rdfs:label "protected" ;
    rdfs:comment "Whether the source enforces a rule before this branch may be written. What the rule is is not read: an unauthenticated caller is not shown it, and an empty answer would read as 'no rule'." ;
    rdfs:domain tech:Branch ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean .
